From: Christopher Albert <albert@tugraz.at>
Subject: [PATCH 00/23] testsuite: Retrospective Bugzilla-provenance attribution headers

This series adds one- or two-line `! Contributed by ...` /
`! Reduced from github.com/fujitsu/compiler-test-suite ...` header
comments to 26 existing gfortran testcases that were derived from
Bugzilla Comment #0 reducers.  No behavioural change.

Background
----------

A manual Bugzilla-provenance audit on 2026-04-22 (tracked at
https://github.com/krystophny/gcc-dev, meta-repo commit 40f0a94,
issues #139-#165) found that 27 committed or fork-local Fortran
testcases re-use the reporter's Bugzilla Comment #0 reducer without
carrying an in-file attribution line.  Four of the 27 are derivatives
of the Fujitsu Compiler Test Suite (Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception,
GPLv3-compatible, no license conflict); the remaining 23 are small
reducers attached to individual PRs.

The GCC Fortran testsuite convention for attribution is inconsistent
— roughly half of recent pr*.f90 tests carry a "! Contributed by"
line, half do not (compare pr113363.f90, pdt_50.f03 vs pr79524.f90,
pr85352.f90).  Attribution is not strictly required for small
reducers.  This series adds headers retroactively for provenance
safety and completeness, not to correct a compliance defect.

